 "response": "**ANSWER: $2533K**\n\n1. **Authority.** Only Finance Office entries count. All other messages (facilities, engineering, vendor, legal and so on) are ignored, as are Finance entries that don't touch the budget (cost-center codes, receipts, audits).\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** I resolved each chain from its last link backward. Withdrawing a withdrawal restores what it had removed.\n   - #0851 \u2192 #0794 \u2192 #0362 \u2192 #0149 \u2192 #0018 \u2192 #0008 \u2192 #0004 \u2192 #0003: the final state is that #0003 (\u2212$441K) stays withdrawn.\n   - #0667 cancels #0036, so #0017 (+$67K) stays in effect.\n   - #0482 \u2192 #0473 \u2192 #0205 \u2192 #0090 \u2192 #0066 \u2192 #0049: the net result is that #0037 (+$389K) stays in effect.\n   - #1580 cancels #1542, so #1318 (\u2212$474K) stays in effect.\n   - #1433 cancels #1426, so #1358 (\u2212$476K) stays in effect.\n   - #1414 cancels #1365, so #1054 (+$537K) stays in effect.\n   - The other chains were handled the same way. Examples of updates that end up withdrawn: #0029, #0057, #0082, #0211, #0218 and #0324. Examples that stay in effect: #0110, #0232, #0214, #0320 and #0509.\n\n3. **Totals.**\n   - Starting value: $2,470K, set by #0001.\n   - All effective increases and decreases from #0003 to #1600, applied once each in order, net to +$63K.\n   - Final budget: 2,470 + 63 = **$2,533K**.\n\nThis total comes from one pass through the records; I did not do a separate re-check.\n\nANSWER: $2533K",
